Product Requirements Document (PRD): Lali Design Website

Project: Lali Design - Cultural Clothing E-commerce & Rental Platform

Version: 1.0

Date: October 26, 2023

1. Project Summary

Lali Design is a comprehensive web platform for customers who love and wear cultural clothing. It serves as a marketplace for vendors (tailors/designers) to sell or rent their designs and a management tool for business administrators. The system supports online e-commerce, in-store sales via a Point of Sale (POS) system, and custom order management.

2. User Roles & Permissions

Customer: Browses the site, buys/rents products, and places custom orders.

Vendor (Tailor/Designer): Manages their own product listings, tracks their orders, and handles custom requests assigned to them.

Shopkeeper: Uses the website's POS interface to process in-store sales and rentals for walk-in customers.

Admin: Has full oversight and control over the entire platform, including users, all orders, website content, and financial reporting.

3. Functional Requirements
FR-1: Homepage & General Site Features

HP-1: Hero Banner: The homepage must display a large, high-quality banner image with a welcoming headline and a "call-to-action" button (e.g., “Explore Collection”).

HP-2: Product Showcase: The homepage must feature a curated selection of products in a grid or card layout, showing the product image, name, and price.

HP-3: Static Content Sections: The homepage must include sections for "Why Choose Us," "How to Order or Rent," a link to a "Custom Orders" form, a "Contact" section, and an "FAQ" section. All content in these sections must be editable by an Admin.

FR-2: Customer Journey & E-commerce

CUST-1: Product Browsing: Customers must be able to view all products and filter them by Category.

CUST-2: Product Detail View: Clicking a product must lead to a page showing all details: multiple images, description, purchase price, rental price, and vendor information.

CUST-3: Buy/Rent Selection: On the product page, customers must be able to choose between "Buy" or "Rent."

CUST-4: Rental Date Selection: If "Rent" is selected, the customer must be able to choose a RentalStartDate and RentalEndDate from a calendar. Dates that are already booked for that product must be disabled.

CUST-5: Shopping Cart: Customers must be able to add multiple items (for purchase or rent) to a shopping cart.

CUST-6: Checkout: Customers must be able to complete their order by providing shipping/contact information and making a payment.

CUST-7: Order Confirmation: After checkout, the customer must receive an order confirmation via email and on-screen.

CUST-8: Custom Order Form: Customers must be able to access a form to submit custom order requests, including text fields for their ideas and measurements.

FR-3: Vendor Functions

VEND-1: Product Creation: Vendors must have a dashboard where they can add a new product by filling out a form (name, description, prices, images, category).

VEND-2: Product Management: Vendors must be able to view, edit, or delete their own product listings.

VEND-3: Order Tracking: Vendors must be able to see a list of all orders (buy and rent) for their products.

VEND-4: Stock Management: When a product is rented, its status should automatically update to "Rented Out" for the selected dates.

VEND-5: Earnings Report: Vendors must be able to see a simple report of their total sales and rental income.

VEND-6: Custom Order Management: Vendors must be able to view and respond to custom order requests assigned to them.

FR-4: Shopkeeper (Point of Sale - POS) Functions

SHOP-1: In-store Transaction: Shopkeepers must have a simple interface to record a sale or rental for a walk-in customer.

SHOP-2: Product Selection: The POS interface must allow the shopkeeper to search for and select an existing product from the inventory.

SHOP-3: Record Payment: The interface must allow the shopkeeper to enter the total amount paid by the customer.

SHOP-4: Track Inventory: An in-store sale or rental must update the product's status and be logged in the central Orders table, just like an online order.

FR-5: Admin Functions

ADM-1: User Management: Admins must be able to add, edit, or remove any user (Customer, Vendor, Shopkeeper).

ADM-2: Full Order Management: Admins must be able to view and manage all orders from both online and in-store channels.

ADM-3: Inventory Tracking: Admins must be able to see a complete overview of all product inventory and statuses.

ADM-4: Expense Management: Admins must have a dedicated section to add and track business expenses (e.g., wages, materials).

ADM-5: Reporting: Admins must be able to generate reports on income, expenses, and rentals by day, week, or month.

ADM-6: Content Control: Admins must be able to change the homepage banner, featured products, and all other static content.

4. Data Model & Field Specifications

Here are the data tables required to build these features, with their fields and data types.

Table Name	Field Name	Data Type	Description & Constraints
Users	UserID	INTEGER	Primary Key, Auto-increment
	Name	VARCHAR(255)	User's full name. Not null.
	Email	VARCHAR(255)	User's email. Unique. Not null.
	PasswordHash	VARCHAR(255)	Hashed password for security. Not null.
	PhoneNumber	VARCHAR(50)	Optional phone number.
	Role	ENUM	Allowed values: Customer, Vendor, Shopkeeper, Admin. Not null.
	CreatedAt	TIMESTAMP	Auto-generated on creation.
Categories	CategoryID	INTEGER	Primary Key, Auto-increment
	CategoryName	VARCHAR(100)	Name of the category (e.g., "Wedding Attire"). Not null.
	Description	TEXT	Optional description of the category.
Products	ProductID	INTEGER	Primary Key, Auto-increment
	CategoryID	INTEGER	Foreign Key to Categories.CategoryID. Not null.
	VendorID	INTEGER	Foreign Key to Users.UserID (where Role is 'Vendor'). Not null.
	Name	VARCHAR(255)	Product name. Not null.
	Description	TEXT	Detailed product description.
	ImageURL	VARCHAR(2048)	URL to the main product image.
	PurchasePrice	DECIMAL(10, 2)	Price to buy. Can be null if only for rent.
	RentalPrice	DECIMAL(10, 2)	Price to rent. Can be null if only for sale.
	Status	ENUM	Allowed values: Available, Rented Out, Sold. Defaults to Available.
Orders	OrderID	INTEGER	Primary Key, Auto-increment
	CustomerID	INTEGER	Foreign Key to Users.UserID.
	ProductID	INTEGER	Foreign Key to Products.ProductID.
	OrderType	ENUM	Allowed values: Buy, Rent, Walk-in-Sale, Walk-in-Rent.
	TotalAmount	DECIMAL(10, 2)	Final price paid. Not null.
	OrderDate	TIMESTAMP	Auto-generated on creation.
	RentalStartDate	DATE	Null if not a rental.
	RentalEndDate	DATE	Null if not a rental.
	Status	ENUM	Allowed values: Pending, Delivered, Completed, Returned.
CustomOrders	CustomOrderID	INTEGER	Primary Key, Auto-increment
	CustomerID	INTEGER	Foreign Key to Users.UserID.
	AssignedVendorID	INTEGER	Foreign Key to Users.UserID. Can be null initially.
	RequestDetails	TEXT	Customer's description of their desired item.
	Status	ENUM	Allowed values: Submitted, In Progress, Quoted, Completed.
	QuotedPrice	DECIMAL(10, 2)	The price quoted by the vendor. Null until quoted.
Expenses	ExpenseID	INTEGER	Primary Key, Auto-increment
	Description	VARCHAR(255)	What the expense was for (e.g., "Fabric purchase"). Not null.
	Amount	DECIMAL(10, 2)	Cost of the expense. Not null.
	Date	DATE	Date the expense was incurred.
